BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mats-residency-program-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: MATS Residency Program: 6-24 Month Funded AI Safety Resea
 rch (Winter 2027 intake)
DESCRIPTION:The MATS Residency\, announced in August 2026 as a new track al
 ongside the seasonal MATS fellowship\, funds 6 to 24 months of high-indepe
 ndence AI safety research for experienced researchers\, whether already in
  AI safety or moving in from adjacent fields.\n\nOrganisation: MATS (ML Al
 ignment and Theory Scholars)\nLocation: In-person at MATS offices in Berke
 ley\, London\, or Washington DC\; visa support provided where required. Fo
 r experienced researchers with at least one substantial piece of research-
 caliber work.\nAward: USD 155\,000 to 285\,000 per year gross (set by loca
 tion\, seniority\, and experience)\, plus medical/dental/vision/life insur
 ance\, retirement plan\, paid time off\, conference funding\, catered meal
 s\, and up to USD 25\,000 relocation support. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: 6 to 24 months with rolling start dates\; three intake windows per year
 .\n\nMore: https://www.matsprogram.org/residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.matsprogram.org/residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:In-person at MATS offices in Berkeley\, London\, or Washington DC\
 ; visa support provided where required. For experienced researchers with a
 t least one substantial piece of research-caliber work.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:braid-creative-commissions-a-promise-in-return-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: BRAID Creative Commissions 2027: A Promise in Return (Res
 ponsible AI\, GBP 8\,000-12\,000\, Edinburgh Art Festival)
DESCRIPTION:BRAID\, the UKRI AHRC-funded Responsible AI programme at the Un
 iversity of Edinburgh\, is commissioning around seven creative works that 
 treat Responsible AI as a question of relationships\, commitments and obli
 gations rather than a technical checklist or a set of rules\, under the ti
 tle A Promise in Return.\n\nOrganisation: BRAID (Bridging Responsible AI D
 ivides)\, University of Edinburgh\, with Inspace\, the Institute for Desig
 n Informatics and the Edinburgh Futures Institute\nLocation: UK. For UK-ba
 sed creative practitioners\; work is presented in Edinburgh during the Edi
 nburgh Art Festival\, August 2027.\nAward: Around seven commissions with b
 udgets of GBP 8\,000 to 12\,000 each\, inclusive of VAT and all costs. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Projects run January to August 2027\, presente
 d during the Edinburgh Art Festival in August 2027\, with possible further
  displays through 2028.\n\nMore: https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK. For UK-based creative practitioners\; work is presented in Edi
 nburgh during the Edinburgh Art Festival\, August 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 .\n\nOrganisation: Daiwa Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individu
 als\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running
  projects that connect the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (ty
 pical awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsis
 tence up to GBP 100 per person per day. A contribution\, not full funding.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\; activity can start from late
  May or early June 2027.\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-pr
 izes/daiwa-foundation-small-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costar-southbank-creative-intelligence-award-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART:20261217T133000Z
DTEND:20261217T140000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 GMT: The Creative Intelligence Award 2027 (CoSTAR Na
 tional Lab x Southbank Centre)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 17 Dec 2026 at 14:00 GMT.\n\nA new co-commission from Co
 STAR National Lab and Southbank Centre to take a creative technology idea 
 that is ready to be completed\, honed or technically advanced through focu
 sed R&D\, then present it to audiences at Southbank Centre's Creative Inte
 lligence festival in autumn 2027.\n\nOrganisation: CoSTAR National Lab and
  Southbank Centre\, supported by UKRI\nLocation: UK (lead applicant must b
 e a UK-registered company\; project activity UK-based). Prototyping at Pin
 ewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Centre\, London.\nAward: GBP 50\,000
  grant (one award)\, plus up to GBP 25\,000 in AI compute and cloud credit
 s\, 2 x 5 days studio access at Pinewood Studios\, a six-week CoSTAR proto
 typing team sprint\, 3 days pre-show testing\, Southbank curatorial and pr
 oducing support\, and 20 hours of mentorship. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: R&D development through 2027\, presented at Creative Intelligence festi
 val\, Southbank Centre\, autumn 2027\n\nMore: https://www.costarnetwork.co
 .uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.costarnetwork.co.uk/calls/the-creative-intelligence-award?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK (lead applicant must be a UK-registered company\; project activ
 ity UK-based). Prototyping at Pinewood Studios\; showcase at Southbank Cen
 tre\, London.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
